<name>Power Window System</name>
<para id="RM0000005DQ00SX" category="J" type-id="301BM" name-id="752B5-00" from="200612">
<dtccode/>
<dtcname>Driver Side Door Glass AUTO UP/DOWN Does Not Operate (Manual Operation Is Possible)</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM0000005DQ00SX_01" type-id="31" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___000024900000">
<name>Circuit Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<ptxt>If AUTO does not function, the fail-safe function may be operating. In addition, AUTO will not function if the registration setting (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM000002FNJ005X"/>) of the power window regulator motor assembly RH (driver side), which is performed after repair, has not been performed.</ptxt>
<atten3>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>The power window system uses the Body Electronics Area Network. First, follow "How to Proceed with Troubleshooting" to perform the "communication function inspection" and confirm that there is no malfunction in the communication system before proceeding with troubleshooting.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>If the power window regulator motor assembly RH (driver side) has been replaced with a new one, perform the registration setting of the power window system. (see <xref label="Seep02" href="RM000002FNJ005X"/>)</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten3>
<atten4>
<ptxt>If there is a malfunction in the pulse sensor in the power window regulator motor assembly RH (driver side), the fail-safe function operates. During fail-safe, remote operation of each window and AUTO operation are disabled. (Only AUTO UP hold and manual down operation are possible)</ptxt>
</atten4>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM0000005DQ00SX_02" type-id="32" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___000024A00000">
